## Consulting / Teaching Reuse

- The **PSALSAR/TCCM protocol diagram** (Fig. 1, article-selection funnel) is directly reusable as a methods slide for explaining SLR rigor to doctoral committee/practitioner audiences.
- The **CRO-centrality gap** is a reusable talking point for board-level AI governance discussions: "if even traditional CRO reporting-line research is underdeveloped, AI risk-ownership reporting lines are almost certainly under-governed" — a strong CISO/CRO audience hook.
- The **India-as-underrepresented-jurisdiction finding (5/151 studies)** is a reusable evidence point for framing the "India gap" in both risk-governance and AI-governance scholarship — useful in proposal/grant narratives and LinkedIn thought-leadership on why India-specific AI governance research matters.

